Usages:
  serializable_data: |
    A plain, immutable data class implementing java.io.Serializable so instances can cross
    process/IPC boundaries (e.g. Android Bundle extras) unchanged.

Annotations: |
  This cell holds the single domain-level value object for a manga's remote tracking state on
  one tracking service (MyAnimeList, AniList, Kitsu, etc.). It has no behavior of its own — it is
  read and written wholesale by the repository and mapping layers.

  Use `serializable_data` for implementation.

---

"Track(id: Long, mangaId: Long, trackerId: Long, remoteId: Long, libraryId: Long?, title: String, lastChapterRead: Double, totalChapters: Long, status: Long, score: Double, remoteUrl: String, startDate: Long, finishDate: Long, private: Boolean)":
  location: Track.kt
  annotations: |
    One manga's synced state with one remote tracking service.

    id: local database row id
    `mangaId`: id of the Manga this track entry belongs to
    `trackerId`: id of the tracking service, matching the id of a tracker registered in the
    app's tracker-registry cell
    `remoteId`: the entry's id on the remote service
    `libraryId`: the entry's id within the user's remote list/library, if the service distinguishes it from `remoteId`
    `title`: title as known by the remote service
    `lastChapterRead`: highest chapter number marked read remotely
    `totalChapters`: total chapters as known by the remote service, 0 if unknown
    status: remote status code (reading/completed/on-hold/etc.), meaning defined per-tracker
    `score`: user's score on the remote service, in that service's own scale
    `remoteUrl`: URL of the entry on the remote service
    `startDate`: epoch millis the user started reading, 0 if unset
    `finishDate`: epoch millis the user finished reading, 0 if unset
    `private`: whether the entry should be excluded from the tracker's public-facing list, when supported

    Use `serializable_data` for implementation.

